/**
* Gmail OAuth callback `reason` → fixed copy.
*
* `/api/client/gmail/oauth-callback` is an UNauthenticated browser navigation
* that redirects to `/client/settings/gmail?gmail=error&reason=<code>`. The
* settings page reflected that parameter verbatim into its error banner, so a
* crafted link put arbitrary attacker-chosen text in front of an authenticated
* customer (React escapes it, so it is text, not markup — but text is enough
* for a "call this number to restore your claim" phish inside the real portal).
*
* The banner must therefore only ever render a literal from this file.
*/
